      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Bouchaville after fur trader William Boucha, the village was renamed Naubinway shortly thereafter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naubinway%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A railroad depot north of Naubinway linked the town to the Upper Peninsula’s lumber boom, boosting export trade.",
